Article 5 The unemployment insurance fund shall consist of the following items:
(1) unemployment insurance premiums paid by urban enterprises and institutions and their employees;
(2) interest on the unemployment insurance fund;
(3) financial subsidies;
(4) other funds incorporated into the unemployment insurance fund according to law.

Article 10 The unemployment insurance fund shall be used for the following expenditures:
(1) unemployment insurance benefits;
(2) medical subsidies during the period of receiving unemployment insurance benefits;
(3) funeral subsidies for unemployed persons who die during the period of receiving unemployment insurance benefits and pension for their dependent spouses and direct relatives;
(4) subsidies for vocational training and job referral during the period of receiving unemployment insurance benefits, the methods and standards of which shall be prescribed by the people's governments of provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities directly under the Central Government;
(5) other expenses related to unemployment insurance as prescribed or approved by the State Council.

Article 14 An unemployed person who meets the following conditions may receive unemployment insurance benefits:
(1) having participated in unemployment insurance according to regulations, and the employer and the person himself/herself have fulfilled the payment obligations for a full year according to regulations;
(2) having interrupted employment not due to his/her own will;
(3) having registered as unemployed and having a job-seeking requirement.
During the period of receiving unemployment insurance benefits, the unemployed person shall also enjoy other unemployment insurance benefits according to regulations.

Article 15 Where an unemployed person falls under any of the following circumstances during the period of receiving unemployment insurance benefits, payment of unemployment insurance benefits shall be suspended, and enjoyment of other unemployment insurance benefits shall also be suspended:
(1) having re-employed;
(2) being enlisted for active military service;
(3) having emigrated abroad;
(4) having enjoyed basic old-age insurance benefits;
(5) being sentenced to criminal detention and put into prison for enforcement or being subjected to re-education through labor;
(6) having refused without justifiable reasons the job referred by the department or agency designated by the local people's government;
(7) other circumstances as provided by laws and administrative regulations.

Article 24 The labor and social security administrative department shall manage the unemployment insurance work and perform the following duties:
(1) implementing unemployment insurance laws and regulations;
(2) guiding the work of social insurance agencies;
(3) supervising and inspecting the collection of unemployment insurance premiums and the payment of unemployment insurance benefits.

Article 25 The social insurance agency shall specifically undertake the unemployment insurance work and perform the following duties:
(1) being responsible for the registration, investigation and statistics of unemployed persons;
(2) being responsible for the management of the unemployment insurance fund according to regulations;
(3) verifying unemployment insurance benefits according to regulations and issuing documents for unemployed persons to receive unemployment insurance benefits and other subsidies from designated banks;
(4) allocating subsidies for vocational training and job referral of unemployed persons;
(5) providing free consultation services to unemployed persons;
(6) other duties that it shall perform as provided by the State.
